   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Position",
     "texto": [
      "Some adjectives change nuance depending on their position: **um grande homem** usually praises a person; **um homem grande** normally describes his size. **Um velho amigo** usually means a friend of long standing; **um amigo velho** can refer to his age. Context decides the meaning."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Intensity and evaluation",
     "texto": [
      "**-íssimo/-íssima** expresses a very high degree: **claríssimo** (very clear). **-inho/-inha** can indicate small size or affection: **uma casinha** (a small or dear house). It isn't always a literal diminutive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
